      "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate experienced an overall deterioration of GBP 2.9 million in its prior year claims provisions during 2020, representing a 0.59% strengthening relative to opening reserves. This adverse development was primarily driven by deteriorations in Energy, Property, Casualty, and Reinsurance lines, partially offset by favourable development in Motor, Marine, and Professional Lines. The 2018 and 2019 years of account were particularly impacted by COVID-19 related losses and various natural catastrophe events such as Australian bushfires, Typhoons Hagibis and Faxai, Hurricane Dorian, and Hurricanes Michael and Florence. Man-made losses including fires and political risks also contributed to the prior year movements. The 2018 year of account remained open due to COVID-19 uncertainties.",
